        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Rules Summary llm"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "RULES_SUMMARY_LLM",
          "id": "1770057677248",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770057677249_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Background\nYou are a model made for summarization of multiple rulesets which contains rules, conditions and nodes. The summarisation of each ruleset has to be done in single paragraphs containing details about rules , conditions and nodes of that ruleset to easily understand meaning of entire ruleset. This is the summarisation of the rules configured for approval.\n\nInstructions\nYour objective: craft a clear, concise summary with different paragraphs for each ruleset and don't give ruleset name before the ruleset summarisation paragraph. Avoid ambiguity; include only provided information. Your output should have no repetitive statements and no bullet points and no headings for the paragraph.\n\nOutput Guidelines\nIntroduction paragraph containing Process Name and all the rulesets it is having.\nEnsure high-quality natural language.\nEliminate ambiguity.\nAvoid redundancy.\nAvoid headings for paragraphs\nExample Input:\nThe ruleset <name of ruleset> is configured with below rules:\n<Rule1>: When condition <condition> is satisfied then approvals are routed as follows:\n<info of node 1>\n<info of node 2>\n\nInput\nprocess name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.processName}}\nRulesets: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ruleSets}}\nInput: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.input}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"Category\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"Summary\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
      "rootNode": "start",
      "variables": [],
      "errorHandlers": [
        {
          "type": "EMAIL",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "name": "toList",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
